    table
      table_row
        table_cell
          paragraph
            text "A"
            text "pipeline"
            text "is a sequence of one or more commands separated by one of the control operators"
            text "|"
            text "or"
            text "|&"
            text ". The format for a pipeline is:"
          paragraph
            text "["
            text "time"
            text "["
            text "-p"
            text "]] [ ! ]"
            text "command1"
            text "[ ["
            text "|"
            text "|"
            text "|&"
            text "]"
            text "command2"
            text "... ]"
          paragraph
            text "The standard output of"
            text "command1"
            text "is connected via a pipe to the standard input of"
            text "command2"
            text ". This connection is performed before any redirections specified by the"
            text "command1"
            text "(see"
            text "REDIRECTION"
            text "below). If"
            text "|&"
            text "is used,"
            text "command1"
            text "'s standard error, in addition to its standard output, is connected to"
            text "command2"
            text "'s standard input through the pipe; it is shorthand for"
            text "2>&1 |"
            text ". This implicit redirection of the standard error to the standard output is performed after any redirections specified by"
            text "command1"
            text "."
          paragraph
            text "The return status of a pipeline is the exit status of the last command, unless the"
            text "pipefail"
            text "option is enabled. If"
            text "pipefail"
            text "is enabled, the pipeline's return status is the value of the last (rightmost) command to exit with a non-zero status, or zero if all commands exit successfully. If the reserved word"
            text "!"
            text "precedes a pipeline, the exit status of that pipeline is the logical negation of the exit status as described above. The shell waits for all commands in the pipeline to terminate before returning a va..."
          paragraph
            text "If the"
            text "time"
            text "reserved word precedes a pipeline, the elapsed as well as user and system time consumed by its execution are reported when the pipeline terminates. The"
            text "-p"
            text "option changes the output format to that specified by POSIX. When the shell is in"
            text "posix mode"
            text ", it does not recognize"
            text "time"
            text "as a reserved word if the next token begins with a `-'. The"
            text "TIMEFORMAT"
            text "variable may be set to a format string that specifies how the timing information should be displayed; see the description of"
            text "TIMEFORMAT"
            text "under"
            text "Shell Variables"
            text "below."

